      "writtenOn": "2021-03-04T05:42:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed in chat, the connectivity mainline module would run in the system_server process so would have the required permissions.\nAnother option would be to use in-process APIs (like ActivityManagerInternal.intentFilterEquals(PendingIntent, PendingIntent)), and adding ActivityManagerInternal to LocalManagerRegistry (JobScheduler still uses the @hide LocalServices.getService). But this adds more infrastructure to maintain and is much harder to test.\n\nConsidering that there is no performance problems as this API isn\u0027t even called when booting a fresh S device (tested with a counter), the current proposal feels like a good tradeoff.\n\nNote that the change moved to ag/13746426 due to the merge conflicts in AOSP.",
